// MASTER COPY - this is the tracked one.  The build copies it to
// Run/Data/Patch.str, which is where the game reads it from and which is
// gitignored, so edit THIS file and rebuild (or copy it across by hand).
//
// Patch.str is the 1.04 string overlay from PatchData.big.  The two original
// strings are kept; everything after them is this fork's.
//
// Comments are '//' - GameText.cpp parseStringFile skips exactly that.

GUI:CustomMission
"CUSTOM MISSION"
END

GUI:StartCustomMission
"START GAME"
END

GUI:Stop
"Stop"
END

GUI:StopDescription
"Stops what the selected units are doing."
END

// The command grid's own attack, hold position and move keys, which stand in no command set:
// the cards they show under the pointer.

GUI:OrderForceAttackDescription
"The next click attacks whatever is under the pointer, the ground and your own side included. Click the key again to call it off."
END

CONTROLBAR:ForceAttack
"&Force Attack"
END

CONTROLBAR:ToolTipForceAttack
"The next click attacks whatever is under the pointer, the ground and your own side included. Click the button again to call it off."
END

GUI:OrderHoldPositionDescription
"The selected units guard the spot they stand on and fight whatever comes near, without chasing it out of the area."
END

GUI:OrderMoveDescription
"The next click on the ground sends the selected units there. Drag instead and they spread out along the line you draw."
END

GUI:SelectionTypeDescription
"Click to keep only these selected. Shift-click to take them out of the selection."
END

GUI:OrderStanceDefensiveDescription
"The selected units shoot what comes into range and hold the ground you put them on. Click to make them aggressive: they go after any enemy they see."
END

GUI:OrderStanceAggressiveDescription
"The selected units go after any enemy they see and chase it. Click to make them defensive again: they only shoot what comes into range and stay where they are."
END

// Smoke signals.  The three ...Placed lines are what an ally reads; %s is the sender's name.  The
// ...Label words are written over the smoke, which is in the sender's colour.
GUI:SignalAttack
"Signal: Attack"
END

GUI:SignalDefend
"Signal: Defend"
END

GUI:SignalAttention
"Signal: Look Here"
END

GUI:SignalAttackPlaced
"%s: attack here!"
END

GUI:SignalDefendPlaced
"%s: defend here!"
END

GUI:SignalAttentionPlaced
"%s: look here!"
END

// The money request's line in the allies' chat, in the asker's own language.
GUI:RequestMoneyChat
"I need money!"
END

GUI:GamePaused
"Game paused."
END

GUI:GameResumed
"Game resumed."
END

// The replay strip's pause button while the replay is paused.
GUI:ReplayResume
"Resume"
END

// Skirmish lobby: an opponent seat with no AI behind it (Shift-Ctrl-T takes it over).
GUI:HumanSlot
"Human"
END

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Options screen.  The five page buttons across the top.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GUI:OptionsTabDisplay
"Display"
END

GUI:OptionsTabAudio
"Audio"
END

GUI:OptionsTabControls
"Controls"
END

GUI:OptionsTabInterface
"Interface"
END

GUI:OptionsTabNetwork
"Network"
END

GUI:OptionsTabGraphics
"Graphics"
END

GUI:OptionsTabEffects
"Effects"
END

GUI:Ultra
"Ultra"
END

GUI:TreeSway
"Swaying Trees"
END

TOOLTIP:TreeSway
"Trees and shrubs lean in the wind. Applies from the next map."
END

TOOLTIP:ExtraAnimations
"Buildings rise inside scaffolding while they are built. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:ExtraAnimations
"Building Scaffolding"
END

GUI:Detail
"Detail Preset"
END

GUI:GraphicsQuality
"Performance / Quality"
END

TOOLTIP:GraphicsQuality
"Left is the fastest picture, right the best looking. Dragging it sets the boxes on this page and on Effects, the cheap ones first, and the four presets are points along it. Change a box afterwards and the preset reads Custom. Applies when you press Accept; some settings wait for the next map or the next launch."
END

GUI:DetailNote0
"Every box on, the most particles and thick smoke, and detail never drops in a big fight. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote1
"All the shadows and full-size textures, with the original smoke. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote2
"Flat shadows in place of cast ones and fewer particles, for a modest graphics card. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote3
"No shadows, half-size textures and the fewest particles, for an old machine. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote4
"Your own mix of the boxes on this page and on Effects, or a point on the slider between two presets. Accept keeps it as it is."
END

GUI:Shadows3D
"Cast Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:Shadows3D
"Shadows that units, buildings and trees throw on the ground and on each other. Off turns all of them off, the sun's shadows included, and Infantry Shadows needs it on. Applies when you press Accept; a few shadows only change on the next map."
END

GUI:Shadows2D
"Flat Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:Shadows2D
"The flat dark patch drawn under a unit or a missile that has no cast shadow. Costs little. Applies when you press Accept."
END

TOOLTIP:CloudShadows
"Cloud shadows drift across the ground. Costs little. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:GroundLighting
"Ground Pattern"
END

TOOLTIP:GroundLighting
"A faint pattern of light and dark laid over the ground, so its repeating tiles show less. Costs little. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:SmoothWater
"Soft Shorelines"
END

TOOLTIP:SmoothWater
"Water fades out at the shore instead of ending on a hard line. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:ShowProps
"Trees And Bushes"
END

TOOLTIP:ShowProps
"Trees and bushes on the map. Off helps a slow machine. Network games always show them. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:HeatEffects
"Heat Haze"
END

TOOLTIP:HeatEffects
"Hot air shimmers, as it does over the Microwave Tank's beam. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:BehindBuilding
"Units Behind Buildings"
END

TOOLTIP:BehindBuilding
"A unit hidden behind a building shows through it as a silhouette in its player's colour. Applies when you press Accept."
END

TOOLTIP:NoDynamicLOD
"When the frame rate drops in a big fight, the game thins out effects to keep up. On, it never does: the picture stays full and the frame rate takes the hit."
END

TOOLTIP:LowResSlider
"How sharp the textures are. Lower saves graphics memory on an old card. Applies when you press Accept."
END

TOOLTIP:ParticleCapSlider
"How many particles of smoke, fire and sparks can exist at once. Big fights reach the limit first; lower it if explosions slow the game down. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:TextureFilter
"Texture Filtering"
END

GUI:TextureFilter0
"Bilinear"
END

GUI:TextureFilter1
"Trilinear"
END

GUI:TextureFilter2
"Anisotropic"
END

TOOLTIP:TextureFilter
"How textures are sampled as they recede from the camera. Bilinear is what the game shipped with and makes distant ground shimmer; anisotropic keeps it sharp. Applies the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:Anisotropy
"Anisotropic Samples"
END

TOOLTIP:Anisotropy
"How many samples anisotropic filtering may take. Auto lets the graphics card decide, up to 16. Only used when texture filtering is anisotropic. Applies the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:AnisotropyCardMaximum
"Auto"
END

GUI:TextureResolution
"Texture Resolution"
END

GUI:ParticleLimit
"Particle Limit"
END

GUI:NeverLowerDetail
"Never Lower Detail"
END

