// The gloss after each figure on the card: what it counts, as the card computes it.  Damage is the
// main weapon's primary damage a shot, the weapon that does the most a second; attack speed spreads
// a clip's reload over its shots; range is in world units, 10 to a pathfinding cell, the square the
// placement grid draws; build time counts the player's power and how many factories make the unit.

TOOLTIP:StatHealthHint
"(damage it can take after armor)"
END

TOOLTIP:StatDamageHint
"(main weapon, one shot, before armor)"
END

TOOLTIP:StatAttackSpeedHint
"(shots a second, reloads counted)"
END

TOOLTIP:StatDamagePerSecondHint
"(damage × attack speed)"
END

TOOLTIP:StatRangeHint
"(10 is one square of the placement grid)"
END

TOOLTIP:StatTimeHint
"(with your power and factories now)"
END

// Under the figures: a unit's upgrades, or on an upgrade's card the units it changes.

TOOLTIP:Upgrades
"UPGRADES"
END

TOOLTIP:UpgradeChanges
"CHANGES"
END

TOOLTIP:UpgradesHint
"(without it → with it)"
END

TOOLTIP:UpgradeChangesHint
"(plain unit → with this)"
END

TOOLTIP:UpgradeOwned
"owned"
END

// Peace time - the lobby combo box, its tooltip, the corner countdown and the three things the game
// says while the clock runs.  Tools/peacetime_layout.py selfcheck fails if any of these goes missing.

GUI:PeaceTimeOff
"No Peace Time"
END

GUI:PeaceTimeFormat
"Peace: %d min"
END

TOOLTIP:PeaceTime
"Nobody can attack for this long at the start of the match. Anything that walks up to an enemy command center burns."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeStarted
"Peace time: %d minutes. Nobody can attack until it runs out."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeRemaining
"Peace time ends in %d seconds."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeOver
"Peace time is over."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeHud
"%d:%02d"
END

GUI:PeaceTimeHudLabel
"PEACE"
END

GUI:ListMore
"+%d more"
END

GUI:LobbyTabChat
"Chat"
END

GUI:LobbyTabInfo
"Info"
END

GUI:LobbyTabSettings
"Lobby Settings"
END

GUI:PeaceTimeLabel
"Peace Time"
END

GUI:Superweapons
"Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsAllow
"Allow Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsLimit
"Limit Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsNone
"No Superweapons"
END

TOOLTIP:Superweapons
"How many of each superweapon a player may have standing. Allow: as many as he can pay for. Limit: one each, and four for the USA Superweapon General. No: none at all, except the Superweapon General, who keeps one. He is the exception because his three superweapons are what he pays for a weaker army with."
END

GUI:UnitLimit
"Unit Limit"
END

TOOLTIP:UnitLimit
"840 units shared out evenly between the players: two players get 420 each, eight get 105. Units standing and units waiting in a queue both count, buildings do not. Your own count and your share are in the top right corner during the match."
END

GUI:IncomeSharing
"Share Income"
END

TOOLTIP:IncomeSharing
"What allies split between them. Every payment is divided evenly between the player who earned it and each ally still in the match: an oil derrick paying 200 to one of two allies pays 100 to each. Oil Derricks shares captured derricks only. All Income adds supply runs, hackers and black markets."
END

GUI:IncomeSharingOff
"No Sharing"
END

GUI:IncomeSharingTech
"Oil Derricks"
END

GUI:IncomeSharingAll
"All Income"
END

GUI:TechRespawn
"Tech Respawn"
END

TOOLTIP:TechRespawn
"How long a destroyed tech building lies in ruins before a neutral one stands on the same spot again, at full health and ready to be captured. Oil derricks, refineries, hospitals, artillery platforms, repair bays and reinforcement pads all come back. A unit or a building standing on the spot holds it back until it moves."
END

GUI:TechRespawnOff
"Never"
END

GUI:TechRespawnFormat
"After %d min"
END

GUI:SupplyPileLimit
"Pile Limit"
END

TOOLTIP:SupplyPileLimit
"How many players may gather from one supply dock or supply pile at the same time. With 1, a pile belongs to whoever reaches it first, and every other player's supply trucks, Workers and Chinooks go to another pile or wait at home. Allies count as separate players. A pile is free again a minute after the last load was taken from it."
END

