GUI:ShadowQuality
"Shadow Quality"
END

GUI:ShadowQuality0
"Low"
END

GUI:ShadowQuality1
"Medium"
END

GUI:ShadowQuality2
"High"
END

TOOLTIP:ShadowQuality
"How sharp unit and building shadows are. High takes about 64 MB of video memory, Low frees memory on a weak card. Direct3D 11 only, and not with Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:VolumetricSmoke
"Volumetric Smoke"
END

TOOLTIP:VolumetricSmoke
"Smoke and dust shade the ground, the units and the smoke behind them by how thick they are. Direct3D 11 only, with a small cost in big fights. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:LightingStyle
"Lighting"
END

GUI:LightingStyle0
"Classic"
END

GUI:LightingStyle1
"Reforged"
END

TOOLTIP:LightingStyle
"Reforged gives each map a stronger, warmer sun, darker shade and deeper shadows, keeping its time of day. Classic is the flat light of 2003, and Classic Graphics always uses it. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:SmokeFireLighting
"Smoke Lit By Fire"
END

TOOLTIP:SmokeFireLighting
"Smoke beside a fire takes on its orange light. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:DebrisTrails
"Explosion Debris Trails"
END

TOOLTIP:DebrisTrails
"Blasts throw fragments that trail smoke, and wrecks shed burning shrapnel. Off keeps the original explosions. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:MapLight
"Warm Light and Haze"
END

TOOLTIP:MapLight
"A low afternoon sun that lights the map warmer and casts longer shadows, and a light haze lying still over low ground. Direct3D 11 only. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:TeamGlow
"Team Color Glow"
END

TOOLTIP:TeamGlow
"The bright patches of each side's color on units and buildings glow in that color. Direct3D 11 only. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:WaterFoam
"Water Foam"
END

TOOLTIP:WaterFoam
"Rivers and lakes carry flecks of foam and a band of it along the shore, and the sun's shadows fall on the water. The sea's waves are unchanged. Direct3D 11 and Classic water only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:GroundMarks
"Battle Marks"
END

TOOLTIP:GroundMarks
"Shells and missiles leave burns on the ground, a fallen building leaves a dark stain with cracks in it, a nuke leaves a burnt ring, and tank treads stay dark for longer. They fade over about four minutes. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:Firelight
"Firelight"
END

TOOLTIP:Firelight
"Burning buildings, wrecks and explosions throw a flickering orange light on the ground, the walls and the units around them. It shows most on night maps. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:HemiAmbient
"Sky And Ground Light"
END

TOOLTIP:HemiAmbient
"Models take the map's ambient light from the sky above and the ground below instead of evenly, so a tank's deck is lighter than its belly. Walls keep the light they had and a night map stays dark. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:AmbientOcclusion
"Ambient Occlusion"
END

TOOLTIP:AmbientOcclusion
"Corners and the ground under what stands on it go darker, so a tank sits on the sand instead of hovering over it. Water and the fog of war stay out of it. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:InternalHdr
"Internal HDR Tone Mapping"
END

TOOLTIP:InternalHdr
"Fire, blasts and lasers past white keep their colour on the way to your screen instead of ending in one flat white, and team colours hold a little more of theirs. Ground and walls away from a fire stay as they were. This is inside the game's picture: your monitor still gets a normal image, and an HDR monitor gets no HDR signal. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:Weather
"Weather"
END

TOOLTIP:Weather
"Rain falls, or sand blows on a desert map and snow on a snowy one, and a wind bends the trees and leans the smoke. A map with its own rain or snow keeps it and takes only the wind. Only your picture changes: what units see and hit stays the same, and other players see their own setting. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:WaterSplashes
"Water Splashes"
END

TOOLTIP:WaterSplashes
"A shell, a bomb or a falling body that comes down in water throws up a splash and sends rings across the surface. Only your picture changes: nothing in the game reads it, and other players see their own setting. Direct3D 11 and Classic water only, and off under Classic Graphics. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:Atmosphere
"Atmosphere"
END

TOOLTIP:Atmosphere
"The ground far from the camera fades toward the sky's colour, and where the map ends or the camera lies flat you see a sky by the map's time of day instead of black. The ground near the camera stays clear and fog of war keeps its dark. Only your picture changes: nothing in the game reads it, and other players see their own setting. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics."
END

GUI:SmoothMotion
"Smooth Motion"
END

TOOLTIP:SmoothMotion
"On a screen faster than 60 Hz, units are drawn between their last two positions instead of holding each one until the next. A 60 Hz screen shows no change. Only your picture changes: nothing in the game reads it, and other players see their own setting. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:StructureCollapse
"Collapsing Buildings"
END

TOOLTIP:StructureCollapse
"A destroyed building sinks into the ground under the blast instead of vanishing in one frame, or swapping to its rubble in one. Only your picture changes: it blocks nothing, nothing in the game reads it, and other players see their own setting. Direct3D 11 only, and off under Classic Graphics."
END

GUI:FormationDrag
"Drag Out A Formation"
END

TOOLTIP:FormationDrag
"Dragging with a move, attack move or guard order armed spreads the units along the line you draw."
END

GUI:BuildWithoutWorker
"Build Without A Worker"
END

TOOLTIP:BuildWithoutWorker
"With nothing selected the command bar shows your workers' buildings, and the idle worker nearest the spot goes to build. Off, the bar stays empty until you select a worker, as in 2003."
END

GUI:HealthBarColors
"Health Bar Color"
END

GUI:HealthBarColors0
"Green To Red"
END

GUI:HealthBarColors1
"Player Color"
END

TOOLTIP:HealthBarColors
"Green at full health through yellow to red, or every bar in its owner's color so you see whose it is. Disabled units stay blue."
END

GUI:MenuTransitionSpeed
"Menu Transition Speed"
END

TOOLTIP:MenuTransitionSpeed
"How fast menus slide and fade. 100 is the original speed."
END

GUI:OptionsGroupMenus
"Menus"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupSpeed
"Game Speed"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupReplays
"Replays"
END

GUI:SaveCamera
"Record My Camera"
END

